## 2. API & Data-Access Reality

**Bottom line: there is no realistic programmatic path to consumer points balances in Australia in 2026.** Every major program is closed.

| Program | Public API? | Partner API? | Aggregator partnerships | T&Cs on third-party access |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Everyday Rewards | No | No (Woolworths Group keeps it closed; B2B partner data flows are bespoke) | None known | Prohibits sharing credentials and automated access |
| Flybuys | No | No | None known | Prohibits credential sharing |
| Qantas Frequent Flyer | No consumer balance API; Qantas's developer site has historically focused on flight status / fares for partners, not member data | Restricted partner-only | None for consumer aggregators | T&Cs prohibit credential sharing |
| Velocity | No | No | None known | T&Cs prohibit credential sharing |
| Amex MR | No consumer API in AU | — | AwardWallet has historically supported via login | T&Cs ambiguous; many jurisdictions treat as prohibited |
| Hotels (Marriott, Hilton, IHG, Accor) | No public consumer APIs; Marriott has a developer portal but it is for property/booking partners | — | AwardWallet supports most via login | T&Cs prohibit automated access |

**Aggregator precedent**
- AwardWallet has operated globally for over a decade using credential-based screen-scraping. They have been blocked or rate-limited by various programs at various times (Southwest, Delta, American Airlines have all blocked them in the past). They explicitly disclaim that they may not always work and that programs can ban accounts that use them.
- No Plaid-equivalent exists for loyalty in any jurisdiction; "open loyalty" is talked about but not standardised.

**Australian-specific:**
- The Consumer Data Right (CDR) covers banking and energy, and was expanded toward non-bank lending. Loyalty programs are **not** within CDR scope and there is no current consultation paper signalling they will be — verify with the latest Treasury / ACCC announcements.
- There is no Australian equivalent of the EU's PSD2 for loyalty data.

**Practical implications for the product:**
- v1 must be manual entry + OCR. There is no shortcut.
- Credential-based aggregation should be deferred until you have legal advice, a clear stance on per-program T&Cs, and accepted that some programs will block you.
- Building toward a commercial API partnership with Qantas or Woolworths is theoretically possible (both have partner ecosystems) but would require revenue traction first.

