## Recommendations

**Stage 0 — Before any code (now)**
1. Verify the four hardcoded conversion rates (Everyday Rewards $/pt, Flybuys $/pt, EDR→QFF ratio, Flybuys→Velocity ratio) directly from each program's current public web page on the day you ship v1.
2. Get a written legal memo on credential storage under the Privacy Act and on the contractual position re program T&Cs before any credential-based feature ships.
3. Decide explicitly that v1 is manual + OCR. Don't promise credential aggregation on a public roadmap; it constrains your legal optionality.

**Stage 1 — v1 ship (3-month target)**
4. Launch with the four big programs hardcoded, plus a generic "other" with manual entry.
5. Ship OCR via Tesseract.js, free for all users.
6. Ship Apple Wallet / Google Wallet pass generation as the visible "delight" feature — this is what gets word-of-mouth.
7. Pricing: free up to 5 programs; AU$39/year for unlimited + alerts + cents-per-point valuations.

**Stage 2 — Monetisation (months 4–9)**
8. Add credit card affiliate placements behind opt-in (e.g. "you have 80k Amex MR — see the top 3 ways to redeem, and the top 3 cards to earn more").
9. Publish your own "AU Points Valuations" content monthly to build SEO around Point Hacks queries.
10. Add Velocity / QFF Classic Reward availability search as Premium+ — this is your wedge against AwardWallet.

**Stage 3 — Defensibility (months 9–18)**
11. Approach Qantas Loyalty and Woolworths Loyalty for an official data partnership *only after* you have demonstrated user volume; both organisations have business-development teams for points partners.
12. Evaluate native shell (Capacitor / React Native wrapper) only if PWA distribution caps out.

**Benchmarks that would change the strategy**
- If CDR scope is expanded to loyalty (an announced consultation paper) → fast-track credential-light architecture.
- If a major AU points aggregator launches in 2026 with >$1M funding → consider a content-first repositioning ahead of feature parity.
- If Apple Wallet's loyalty pass API gains live-balance updates (currently `.pkpass` updates are push-only and clunky) → barcode wallet feature becomes a much stronger hook.

