## Caveats

- **Research access on this pass was constrained** by an internal tooling error early in the workflow. The conversion-rate figures — especially the Everyday Rewards → Qantas and Flybuys → Velocity ratios, and the Point Hacks / AFF cents-per-point bands — must be re-verified against each program's current public terms and the latest Point Hacks valuations article before being hardcoded into the product. Partner ratios are the single most likely datapoint to have shifted in the last 12 months.
- **Point Hacks and Australian Frequent Flyer valuations are point-in-time** and shift with each airline devaluation. Treat the cents-per-point ranges above as indicative for product copy, not authoritative for financial advice.
- **The legal section is not legal advice.** The Privacy Act reform process has been moving in stages; while the 10 December 2024 first tranche (Privacy and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2024) and the AU$50M / 3x benefit / 30% turnover penalty regime under the 2022 Act are confirmed, the specific provisions in force in May 2026 (including any second-tranche reforms post-March 2026) must be confirmed with current legal counsel.
- **The competitive landscape for AU-launched 2023–2026 points apps is the area with the thinnest sourcing** — do a targeted scan of the AU App Store, Crunchbase, Product Hunt, and SmartCompany / Startup Daily before launch.
- **Stocard's current AU status** is described based on the July 2021 Klarna acquisition and the subsequent 2022 wind-down of card-wallet functionality; verify whether any product revival has occurred in 2024–2026.
- **CDR scope as of May 2026** — confirm with the Treasury and ACCC consultation registers; the rollout schedule has been revised multiple times and there has been no announced loyalty-sector expansion.
- **Inactivity-based expiry windows** (QFF 18 months, Velocity 24 months, Everyday Rewards 12 months historically) should be re-confirmed in each program's current T&Cs before being used to drive push notifications, because false-alert risk is high if the rules have shifted.